    "summary": "A few of the comments that stood out to us yesterday: \"@Luz_do_sol My obsession with Capris started back in high school when a friend bought a yellow 1972 Capri 2000 with the Décor Group. At the time, I was driving a 1973 Ford pickup, so the Capri was my first real experience with a “foreign car.” It seemed pretty exotic, especially the way it could take corners at twice the posted speed limit. That worked great until my friend wrapped it around a tree. He replaced it with a 1971 Capri 1600, and we swapped the engine and interior from the&#8230;\" 16 CapriRS2800 commented on RS-Style, 2.8L V6-Powered 1974 Mercury Capri 5-Speed \"E39 Tourings really are the peak of utility BMWs. The design is just timeless and I'd love to have this next to my blue non-Alpina 2001 530i Touring (525i M54B30 swap).\" 6 CrzRsn commented on 1998 BMW Alpina B10 3.2 Touring 5-Speed \"I have a 1970 Lotus 7S4 that I race. They are great little cars. This one looks to be a sound, untampered with example. Areas of concern with these cars is rust along the steel side panels where they attach to the lower perimeter frame rails. These areas collect dirt and moisture resulting in rust and structurally compromised chassis. This example seems to be free of this issue. As for replacement drivetrain, Standard 1600 Xflow with 2000e transmission right out of a Cortina is all one needs.&#8230;\" 5 Lotus_Ivan commented on 1971 Lotus Seven Project",
